            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level input TIA branches with DC-overload cancellation must accept inp and inn and preserve the specified input bias and overload behavior.",
            "electrical_reason": "Each input is the emitter of a common-base NPN (XQcbp/XQcbn) with a collector load and an active emitter-follower output. Each branch also has a PMOS comparison/mirror path sensing its input against vref and developing ota_gp/ota_gn; the corresponding shunt NMOS (XMtp/XMtn) removes input DC current under the slow integrating control. This is a genuine DC cancellation path rather than a RF bypass. The nominal and overload input common-mode and mismatch measurements are consistent with both symmetric branches being biased and responsive."
