            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level gain-controlled RF stages must provide monotonic gain control and the specified transimpedance, bandwidth, and group delay.",
            "electrical_reason": "The first differential BJT stage is driven from tia_op/tia_on and buffered onto pkdinp/pkdinn; those nodes directly drive the second differential BJT stage, whose emitter-follower outputs are AC-coupled and rebaised onto bufinp/bufinn. In both stages, the shared emitter/tail node has a fixed sink and a substantial gc-gated NMOS sink (XMv1g/XMv2g), so gc genuinely changes the transconductance/bias of the active RF path. The measured monotonic tuning, nonzero gain span, and bandwidth support that this path is active; gain and group-delay target misses are sizing/performance issues, not evidence of a missing stage."
