            "electrical_reason": "The two RF inputs are capacitively coupled to biased rectifying BJT bases; XQpr/XQnr charge/discharge the rec_p node against Rrecp/Crecp. rec_p then drives one side of the active detector-output BJT pair XQga/XQgb, whose resistive collector loads create detn/detp and whose common tail has an NMOS bias sink. Thus the detector includes real RF input, rectification, stored charge, output, and bias paths. Its measured detector differential response is nonzero and strictly monotonic, although materially smaller than the endpoint targets."
