            "electrical_reason": "Although XQagp/XQagn and XQagef constitute a biased small-signal differential amplifier/follower, detp and detn reach its input bases only through Caga/Cagb. Those capacitors block the detector's DC/averaged differential output, so no detector-responsive averaged control voltage can be conveyed to agc in an operating-point AGC loop. This explains the exactly zero measured AGC gain and is a material missing AGC-control function, not merely a gain-sizing miss."
