            "electrical_reason": "A coherent forward differential signal path does exist from inp/inn through the TIA follower outputs, both RF stages, the AC-coupled buffer inputs, and the active output buffer to finalp/finaln. The nonzero PAM4 output and three positive eye openings corroborate that forward path. However, the required receiver-level AGC loop is not coherently completed: detector outputs detp/detn couple to the AGC inputs only through Caga/Cagb, which cannot convey their averaged control information to agc and hence gc. The constituent detector, AGC, selector, and gain-control functions therefore do not form the required operational complete receiver."
